# Inputs
#   build args:  KERNEL_VERSION (default: 6.12.0), UKI_SIGN_KEY (default: /etc/pki/yubios/uki.key)
#   runtime env: none (UKI runs once at boot)
#   files:       usr/lib/uki/*.efi (built into the image), vmlinuz-* (from build kernel)
#   secrets:     UKI_SIGN_KEY (BuildKit --mount=type=secret,id=uki-sign)
#   prereqs:     systemd-boot, sbctl or pesign for signing
#   precedence:  --build-arg > ENV > built-in default
#   validation:  KERNEL_VERSION must match a vmlinuz-* in the build root
#   failure:     uki-build step exits 1 with the missing kernel version


# Failure modes -- cycle 14

# Cycle-14 NSS-failure-modes gap-closure. Each row pairs severity with probability;
# detection signal + recovery path + fault-injection test are required.
# See skills/github-yubios-KS9n5GAT/nss-failure-modes/SKILL.md for the taxonomy.
#
#   FM-001 [CRITICAL, Rare]  UKI signed with wrong key; bootc refuses to load
#     why:        signing key in /etc/pki/yubios does not match secure-boot DB
#     detection:  boot fails with "signature verification failed"; sbctl status red
#     recovery:   sign with correct key; update DB; rebuild UKI
#     prevent:    pre-flight sbctl status; pin signing key fingerprint
#     test:       sign with known-bad key; assert UKI rejected
#
# Envelope: severity 1-2 negligible, 3-4 degraded, 5-6 operational,
# 7-8 major (outage/data loss/security), 9-10 critical.
# Probability is evidence-based; cite the denominator.

